1
00:01:40,159 --> 00:01:41,079
They're always talking about

2
00:01:42,319 --> 00:01:43,319
a war breaking out,

3
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:45,280
but people in Taipei and over here

4
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:47,120
still have to live normal lives,

5
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:48,319
still have to keep on living.

6
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:50,760
Even if the sky falls, so what?

7
00:01:51,239 --> 00:01:52,920
If anything's wrong, you can tell me.

8
00:01:56,319 --> 00:01:57,040
Who is it?

9
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:03,719
Is someone forcing you to do something?

10
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:05,040
Are they?

11
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:17,800
What on earth happened?

12
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:22,319
The nightclub...

13
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,240
me...

14
00:02:25,879 --> 00:02:27,639
that man my aunt is with...

15
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:29,159
and me...

16
00:02:29,919 --> 00:02:32,680
everything between you and me...

17
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:35,199
They know it all.

18
00:02:37,319 --> 00:02:39,000
My whole family found out.

19
00:02:39,439 --> 00:02:41,560
I can't go back anywhere now.

20
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:44,759
I can't go back anywhere.

21
00:02:45,919 --> 00:02:47,800
I have nowhere left to go.

22
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:54,000
I really don't know what to do.

23
00:02:58,039 --> 00:02:59,400
It's okay. It's okay.

24
00:03:06,199 --> 00:03:07,039
It's all right.

25
00:03:11,039 --> 00:03:12,039
It doesn't matter.

26
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:15,520
Life goes on just the same.

27
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:16,879
Right?

28
00:03:20,599 --> 00:03:22,280
You're still my secretary.

29
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:23,560
Come to work tomorrow as usual.

30
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:25,199
As for the nightclub, don't go anymore.

31
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:30,960
Sister Xia is a good person.

32
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:33,439
I can't be a bad person.

33
00:03:35,759 --> 00:03:37,159
What makes someone a good person?

34
00:03:37,759 --> 00:03:38,879
What makes someone a bad person?

35
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:40,680
Sister Xia is a good person.

36
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:42,960
And you're a good person, too.

37
00:03:58,680 --> 00:03:59,960
So what happened to that poet later,

38
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:02,400
and his muse?

39
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:10,039
He stayed at a frontline field hospital.

40
00:04:10,639 --> 00:04:12,159
Besides caring for the sick every day,

41
00:04:13,199 --> 00:04:14,840
he dug graves for the dead,

42
00:04:15,719 --> 00:04:18,920
and wrote to the girl he loved.

43
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,680
Countless letters every day.

44
00:04:22,439 --> 00:04:23,240
Later,

45
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:25,000
the two of them got married

46
00:04:26,519 --> 00:04:27,839
and had a daughter.

47
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:29,920
That sounds nice.

48
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:32,759
Later, they split up,

49
00:04:34,319 --> 00:04:35,800
and each fell in love with someone new.

50
00:04:36,759 --> 00:04:37,600
Then tell me...

51
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:40,399
what they had before,

52
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:42,199
was it ever real?

53
00:05:20,639 --> 00:05:21,439
Great.

54
00:05:21,439 --> 00:05:22,759
Now I definitely can't sleep.

55
00:05:23,959 --> 00:05:24,759
It's all your fault.

56
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:27,720
What are they saying?

57
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,160
Still reading poetry?

58
00:05:30,839 --> 00:05:33,800
"If you had the chance to go back ten years,

59
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:35,959
would you still want to become who you are now?"

60
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:38,600
Who's asking?

61
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,920
Jin Lina asked Lin Kanshan.

62
00:05:42,319 --> 00:05:43,319
I want to ask you, too.

63
00:05:46,639 --> 00:05:48,120
If you had the chance,

64
00:05:48,639 --> 00:05:50,560
would you still choose this job?

65
00:05:59,639 --> 00:06:00,720
I don't know either.

66
00:06:02,079 --> 00:06:04,000
I'd always heard wiretapping is the most grueling.

67
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,680
Watching the machine count the seconds,

68
00:06:07,639 --> 00:06:08,879
listening to the rain,

69
00:06:08,879 --> 00:06:10,399
counting cracks on the wall...

70
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:13,519
I was practically turning into a block of wood.

71
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:15,839
But it's better now.

72
00:06:16,319 --> 00:06:17,560
Lin Kanshan is back.

73
00:06:19,399 --> 00:06:21,120
It's like suddenly having a target,

74
00:06:21,279 --> 00:06:22,360
having a direction.

75
00:06:22,959 --> 00:06:24,439
Maybe it really is like you said:

76
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:27,319
herbal medicine only works after it simmers long enough.

77
00:06:28,519 --> 00:06:29,560
Right now, I feel like

78
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:30,959
sticking it out like this is pretty nice.

79
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,360
No need to think about anything else.

80
00:06:34,519 --> 00:06:36,160
If we'd taken a different path,

81
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:38,720
we definitely never would've met in this lifetime.

82
00:06:39,639 --> 00:06:41,000
It's nice as it is now.

83
00:06:41,759 --> 00:06:43,000
Under the same roof,

84
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,279
listening to the same rain.

85
00:06:46,079 --> 00:06:48,040
Could I be a poet, too?

86
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:54,319
You're actually not dull at all.

87
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:56,639
Sometimes you're pretty romantic.

88
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:03,560
Everyone says we're just acting,

89
00:07:04,879 --> 00:07:05,959
but I can't fake it.

90
00:07:08,399 --> 00:07:10,160
I know you don't like milk,

91
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:11,680
you love spicy food,

92
00:07:12,439 --> 00:07:14,519
and when you're sick, you drink ginger tea with no sugar.

93
00:07:14,959 --> 00:07:16,639
I memorized all of that long ago.

94
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:18,040
How could that be an act?

95
00:07:18,680 --> 00:07:19,839
I haven't been acting for a long time either.

96
00:07:23,439 --> 00:07:24,120
Let's go.

97
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:47,639
Please have a seat inside.

98
00:07:47,639 --> 00:07:48,560
Thanks for coming.

99
00:07:51,439 --> 00:07:53,920
Please, come in.

100
00:07:55,079 --> 00:07:56,240
Thank you, thank you.

101
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:57,000
President.

102
00:07:57,720 --> 00:07:59,639
Look who I brought with me.

103
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:00,639
Boss Ding!

104
00:08:00,639 --> 00:08:01,920
Long time no see.

105
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:02,920
With the President here,

106
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:04,120
we can do some business together.

107
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:05,360
Great. It's a deal, then.

108
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:06,279
Head table, head table.

109
00:08:06,279 --> 00:08:07,000
Come, right this way.

110
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,079
All right, we'll talk later.

111
00:08:08,079 --> 00:08:09,040
Talk later. Have a few drinks tonight!

112
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:09,600
Boss Lin.

113
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:10,959
Brother Cai.

114
00:08:10,959 --> 00:08:11,959
Congratulations!

115
00:08:11,959 --> 00:08:12,879
Sign in over here, please.

116
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:14,560
Boss Ding, Boss Wen.

117
00:08:16,759 --> 00:08:17,360
Please head inside.

118
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:18,160
This way, please.

119
00:08:22,759 --> 00:08:24,000
Look out for us.

120
00:08:24,279 --> 00:08:25,519
A real estate firm, huh?

121
00:08:25,519 --> 00:08:27,000
We're in the same trade!

122
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,600
We must exchange experiences.

123
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:29,120
Definitely, definitely.

124
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:29,800
We'll talk later.

125
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,199
Have a few drinks tonight!

126
00:08:31,199 --> 00:08:32,000
Come, right this way.

127
00:08:33,039 --> 00:08:34,200
Boss Lin, congratulations!

128
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:34,960
Thank you, thank you.

129
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:35,759
Sign here, please.

130
00:08:35,879 --> 00:08:37,519
Brothers, I've been waiting for you!

131
00:08:37,519 --> 00:08:38,879
Brother Shan, congratulations!

132
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:41,919
That tie looks really sharp.

133
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:44,240
Strait Blue. You gave it to me, after all.

134
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:45,000
Great taste, right?

135
00:08:45,799 --> 00:08:47,279
Boss Lin, congratulations!

136
00:08:47,279 --> 00:08:48,080
Sister Lan!

137
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,759
It's an honor to have you here.

138
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:50,919
Come, right this way.

139
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:52,200
Please go on in.

140
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,000
This way, please.

141
00:08:53,399 --> 00:08:54,320
Have a few more drinks tonight!

142
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:54,759
Will do.

143
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:00,759
Brother Qi!

144
00:09:00,759 --> 00:09:01,559
Brother!

145
00:09:01,559 --> 00:09:03,039
How long has it been since we last met?

146
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:05,080
Long time no see! Long time no see!

147
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:08,200
Brother Qi, you're doing so well for yourself these days.

148
00:09:08,399 --> 00:09:11,200
I heard you brought back a huge amount of capital this time.

149
00:09:11,559 --> 00:09:12,559
More money than you can count.

150
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:15,080
Just how big are you planning to make your business?

151
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:17,000
The mainland is developing so fast.

152
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:18,559
Having all the money in the world is useless...

153
00:09:18,559 --> 00:09:19,840
...without the right projects, you know.

154
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:21,960
Brother Qi, our fortunes align!

155
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:24,240
You've got to take your brother along on good projects!

156
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:25,519
What do you say?

157
00:09:25,639 --> 00:09:26,919
Making money is all you think about.

158
00:09:26,919 --> 00:09:27,679
Are you married yet?

159
00:09:27,679 --> 00:09:28,600
Who has the time?

160
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:30,320
There's so much to deal with every day.

161
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:33,639
Tonight, you're entering the bridal chamber!

162
00:09:33,639 --> 00:09:34,559
Consider it done.

163
00:09:34,559 --> 00:09:36,080
A new bride every night would be even better!

164
00:09:37,919 --> 00:09:38,600
Come on, Brother Qi.

165
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:39,879
Have a seat over here.

166
00:09:40,039 --> 00:09:42,080
Come, come, come.

167
00:09:42,240 --> 00:09:44,200
Come on over.

168
00:09:47,679 --> 00:09:49,399
Mr. Lin is our bellwether now.

169
00:09:49,399 --> 00:09:50,919
We're just little lambs following behind.

170
00:09:50,919 --> 00:09:52,399
Help your brother out when you get the chance.

171
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:53,440
Boss Ding.

172
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:55,000
He's the real big brother here.

173
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,200
We all have to follow his lead.

174
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:58,399
Back then, my factory site was just wasteland.

175
00:09:58,480 --> 00:09:59,679
Not even a blade of grass grew there.

176
00:09:59,679 --> 00:10:00,480
And look at it now!

177
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:02,720
It's the best industrial park in the whole province.

178
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:04,360
Who would've thought it'd develop so fast?

179
00:10:04,360 --> 00:10:05,799
The government relocated to the north.

180
00:10:05,799 --> 00:10:07,120
We just got lucky.

181
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:09,080
From now on, I'll follow Brother Wu.

182
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,799
If Brother Wu tells me to eat dirt, I'll eat it.

183
00:10:10,799 --> 00:10:12,480
Because that dirt definitely has miracle fertilizer in it!

184
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:15,000
Brother Wu, let me toast you.

185
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,399
Just lead me to some grass from now on!

186
00:10:16,399 --> 00:10:17,799
You used to ignore me back then.

187
00:10:17,799 --> 00:10:18,759
No way, no way, not at all!

188
00:10:18,759 --> 00:10:19,519
Just kidding!

189
00:10:19,519 --> 00:10:20,679
Come on, drink up, drink up!

190
00:10:20,679 --> 00:10:21,480
Bottoms up!

191
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:24,480
I need to head over there and propose a toast.

192
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:25,639
Let's go, let's go.

193
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:26,840
Let's all go together.

194
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:27,679
Let's go, let's go.

195
00:10:27,799 --> 00:10:28,639
Come on, let's go.

196
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:30,440
Please look out for us.

197
00:10:32,759 --> 00:10:33,759
Let's propose a toast first.

198
00:10:34,679 --> 00:10:36,000
Come, come, come.

199
00:10:37,279 --> 00:10:38,919
When he was calling from home,

200
00:10:38,919 --> 00:10:40,879
didn't he constantly curse this Boss Ding?

201
00:10:40,879 --> 00:10:42,159
Without ever repeating an insult.

202
00:10:42,159 --> 00:10:43,799
Now he's acting like a completely different person.

203
00:10:45,519 --> 00:10:47,200
The nicer someone is to you on the surface,

204
00:10:47,519 --> 00:10:49,000
the more they're plotting against you.

205
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:50,879
That's usually how it goes.

206
00:10:51,399 --> 00:10:52,279
Don't you think?

207
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:54,679
It's just superficial pleasantries.

208
00:10:54,679 --> 00:10:55,919
Still gotta play along.

209
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:56,840
Here.

210
00:11:00,679 --> 00:11:01,759
I'm going to the restroom.

211
00:11:08,399 --> 00:11:12,200
So, taken up running marathons lately?

212
00:11:14,159 --> 00:11:15,000
What do you mean?

213
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:17,159
You and Jinlan.

214
00:11:17,399 --> 00:11:18,279
A relationship marathon.

215
00:11:18,279 --> 00:11:19,399
You've been at it for so long,

216
00:11:19,399 --> 00:11:20,759
and still have no plans to get married?

217
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:23,600
I was planning to propose,

218
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:24,519
but I wasn't sure if...

219
00:11:24,519 --> 00:11:26,559
I should apply to the department first.

220
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:30,639
Cook the dish first, serve it, then apply.

221
00:11:30,919 --> 00:11:32,720
What boss would make you take it back then?

222
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:33,960
Just don't spend all that time fussing,

223
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:35,440
only to find the pot leaking in the kitchen.

224
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:37,759
You're just so rigid.

225
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,519
You have to ask about everything.

226
00:11:39,519 --> 00:11:41,639
Believe me, if Huadong hadn't been injured

227
00:11:41,639 --> 00:11:43,240
and had been monitoring with Jinlan,

228
00:11:43,559 --> 00:11:44,759
their kid would probably be a month old by now.

229
00:11:47,279 --> 00:11:48,919
Actually, we already have a plan.

230
00:11:49,799 --> 00:11:51,879
If couples aren't allowed in the same division,

231
00:11:51,879 --> 00:11:52,960
I'll apply for a transfer.

232
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:54,759
And if the department says no?

233
00:11:54,759 --> 00:11:56,360
Jinlan said she'd resign.

234
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:58,480
I think she's better at the job than I am.

235
00:11:58,759 --> 00:11:59,759
I should be the one to quit.

236
00:12:01,879 --> 00:12:02,879
I've thought it through.

237
00:12:02,879 --> 00:12:03,679
If I quit,

238
00:12:03,679 --> 00:12:05,960
at worst, I can rent out medical equipment.

239
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:07,480
Failing that,

240
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:10,120
I'll go give Lin Kanshan a hand at his company.

241
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:11,120
Cultivate connections,

242
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:12,399
and still make myself useful.

243
00:12:12,679 --> 00:12:13,799
Come on, come on!

244
00:12:17,639 --> 00:12:18,799
To a prosperous business!

245
00:12:18,799 --> 00:12:20,159
Let's strike it rich together!

246
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:21,519
Congratulations on the grand opening!

247
00:12:21,919 --> 00:12:23,200
Didn't you bring him a gift?

248
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:25,440
Of course I have a gift.

249
00:12:26,279 --> 00:12:27,399
When the time is right.

250
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:08,639
What I told you last time...

251
00:13:08,840 --> 00:13:11,519
Track down where all of Wen Zongshu's funds went,

252
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:13,759
including who he's been in contact with lately.

253
00:13:14,039 --> 00:13:15,039
Keep this in mind.

254
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:16,559
Don't worry, don't worry, I will.

255
00:13:26,279 --> 00:13:27,960
So regarding what I told you,

256
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:28,759
you must remember it.

257
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:31,279
Report to me immediately if anything comes up.

258
00:13:31,279 --> 00:13:31,960
Got it?

259
00:13:32,519 --> 00:13:33,240
Understood.

260
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:34,600
I'll keep you posted.

261
00:13:41,799 --> 00:13:42,919
Distinguished guests,

262
00:13:43,279 --> 00:13:46,919
North Wind International Garment Trading Co., Ltd.'s

263
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:48,559
groundbreaking ceremony

264
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:51,399
begins now.

265
00:13:57,559 --> 00:13:58,720
The ribbon-cutting

266
00:13:59,399 --> 00:14:00,679
starts now.

267
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:37,279
You know,

268
00:14:37,559 --> 00:14:40,120
parking under the shade has its pros and cons.

269
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:41,519
Keeps it out of the sun,

270
00:14:41,799 --> 00:14:43,320
but there's way too much bird poop.

271
00:14:43,679 --> 00:14:45,200
I'll need to give the car a good wash this afternoon.

272
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:47,279
Are you this diligent at home too?

273
00:14:47,279 --> 00:14:49,039
Are you a neat freak, or did Jinlan ask you to?

274
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:51,600
Isn't washing the car too clean a bad idea?

275
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:53,759
It makes it stand out too easily.

276
00:14:55,879 --> 00:14:57,480
Washing it a lot is fine.

277
00:14:57,639 --> 00:14:59,279
Overthinking things isn't.

278
00:14:59,879 --> 00:15:00,960
Have you ever heard that

279
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:02,320
constantly washing your hands

280
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:04,080
means you've got a dirty conscience?

281
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:05,679
Is that so?

282
00:15:07,919 --> 00:15:08,879
Before, during, and after the meal,

283
00:15:08,879 --> 00:15:10,039
you washed your hands three times.

284
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:11,600
When you went to the restroom,

285
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:13,919
were you tailing me, or Boss Ding?

286
00:15:17,799 --> 00:15:18,799
Between him and me,

287
00:15:18,799 --> 00:15:20,240
which one's the germ on your hands?

288
00:15:22,559 --> 00:15:24,200
If it were germs, that'd be easy.

289
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:25,919
If it's a virus, that's trouble.

290
00:15:27,639 --> 00:15:28,639
It was Wen Zongshu.

291
00:15:29,279 --> 00:15:31,519
Before you and Boss Ding went to the restroom,

292
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:33,960
Wen Zongshu gave someone in there

293
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:34,960
a few SIM cards.

294
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:37,159
I couldn't see exactly how many.

295
00:15:38,559 --> 00:15:40,000
Phone cameras just don't cut it.

296
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:40,840
Too blurry.

297
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:42,919
Not as good as Xiao Lu's camera.

298
00:15:42,919 --> 00:15:43,960
He went too?

299
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,200
The mantis stalks the cicada...

300
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:47,720
You were watching someone else,

301
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:49,159
while he was watching Lin Kanshan.

302
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:50,639
For just a simple meal,

303
00:15:50,639 --> 00:15:52,360
everyone had their own target.

304
00:15:53,519 --> 00:15:54,159
Interesting.

305
00:15:54,879 --> 00:15:56,360
So what's Boss Ding's deal?

306
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:01,240
What if I said it was a coincidence?

307
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:03,480
Just looking for a bathroom buddy.

308
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:08,919
I'm just curious.

309
00:16:08,919 --> 00:16:10,279
Take Boss Lin, for example.

310
00:16:10,279 --> 00:16:12,600
He used to want to hire a hitman to kill Boss Ding,

311
00:16:13,039 --> 00:16:14,840
but now he invites him to the opening.

312
00:16:14,960 --> 00:16:16,799
And Boss Ding actually dared to show up.

313
00:16:17,080 --> 00:16:18,720
As long as there's money to make,

314
00:16:18,919 --> 00:16:20,440
could they even open a factory together?

315
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:21,879
Friends today, enemies tomorrow.

316
00:16:22,399 --> 00:16:23,360
Aren't people always like that?

317
00:16:23,559 --> 00:16:24,320
A gun gets pulled,

318
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:25,440
pressed right against someone's head,

319
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:26,720
finger about to pull the trigger...

320
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,519
Yet as long as the payoff is big enough,

321
00:16:28,519 --> 00:16:29,639
they'll still work together

322
00:16:29,799 --> 00:16:31,000
and become sworn brothers.

323
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:34,039
Loyalty

324
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:36,360
only exists if the price to betray is low.

325
00:16:36,679 --> 00:16:37,320
Is that so?

326
00:16:38,919 --> 00:16:39,720
Isn't it?

327
00:16:44,639 --> 00:16:46,240
Humans are strange creatures.

328
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:48,519
Inside, they'd love to see you dead,

329
00:16:48,519 --> 00:16:49,600
yet they keep on smiling.

330
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,080
Never mind those two.

331
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:52,360
Who isn't like that?

332
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:58,039
Humans are such strange creatures.

333
00:17:58,200 --> 00:17:59,519
Wishing you dead on the inside,

334
00:17:59,640 --> 00:18:00,640
yet smiling right to your face.

335
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,160
It's not just the two of them.

336
00:18:04,799 --> 00:18:05,720
Aren't we all like that?

337
00:19:22,559 --> 00:19:24,960
Besides "Oppose Taiwan Independence, Save Taiwan, China,"

338
00:19:25,279 --> 00:19:27,559
did they have any other slogans?

339
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:30,960
Don't give me that nonsense.

340
00:19:31,680 --> 00:19:33,000
Afraid of offending someone?

341
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:35,839
No, that's not it.

342
00:19:36,279 --> 00:19:37,799
Are the activities of this union

343
00:19:38,519 --> 00:19:39,640
and the other demonstrations

344
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:40,839
really the same thing?

345
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,359
Don't come at me

346
00:19:43,359 --> 00:19:44,960
with all this useless chatter.

347
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:45,400
Okay.

348
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:46,720
I'll take care of it.

349
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:51,440
Zhu Yingjia.

350
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:52,119
Here, sir!

351
00:19:54,960 --> 00:19:56,119
Intel from Minzhong says

352
00:19:56,920 --> 00:19:58,480
a State Security internal bulletin reported

353
00:19:58,480 --> 00:20:00,400
that A-bian wants a "referendum,"

354
00:20:01,039 --> 00:20:02,480
and the Americans will apply pressure.

355
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:07,880
Our operative inside the MIB

356
00:20:07,880 --> 00:20:08,960
just confirmed that

357
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:11,920
the notice from our municipal and provincial bureaus

358
00:20:12,359 --> 00:20:13,920
in under 24 hours

359
00:20:14,279 --> 00:20:16,160
was already on desks in Taipei.

360
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:17,880
A deliberate leak.

361
00:20:22,160 --> 00:20:23,119
How many times did you verify this?

362
00:20:23,119 --> 00:20:24,079
This is the second time.

363
00:20:24,359 --> 00:20:25,720
If the first time was a coincidence,

364
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:27,519
this time confirms it beyond doubt.

365
00:20:28,119 --> 00:20:29,400
We've tracked down the channel too.

366
00:20:29,680 --> 00:20:31,440
It's still Pacific Nightclub.

367
00:20:31,799 --> 00:20:32,640
That place

368
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:35,920
is one of the fastest intel hubs in the city.

369
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:37,519
Is it that person?

370
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:40,039
Most likely.

371
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:53,319
The Party

372
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:55,799
groomed that person in vain.

373
00:21:00,519 --> 00:21:01,519
When do we make the arrest?

374
00:21:07,279 --> 00:21:08,559
When you say "high probability,"

375
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:10,599
what percentage is that?

376
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:18,799
It's almost certain.

377
00:21:19,759 --> 00:21:21,160
I want 100 percent certainty.

378
00:21:57,160 --> 00:21:58,119
Had another dream.

379
00:22:12,119 --> 00:22:14,200
You can't let it go.

380
00:22:15,480 --> 00:22:17,200
You still suspect Ma Qi is dirty.

381
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:19,839
Found any evidence?

382
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:24,680
Then why are you still obsessing over that yarn?

383
00:22:26,319 --> 00:22:27,640
Just because over the past few years,

384
00:22:27,920 --> 00:22:29,599
he kept dealing with shady people,

385
00:22:30,599 --> 00:22:32,200
you suspect he was bought by the enemy?

386
00:22:33,319 --> 00:22:34,440
He wouldn't be bought.

387
00:22:35,039 --> 00:22:36,400
A traitor's motives are usually

388
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:40,079
money, sex, danger, or ideology.

389
00:22:40,720 --> 00:22:42,400
But there's another type that's the hardest to handle.

390
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:43,440
They think very highly of themselves,

391
00:22:43,839 --> 00:22:45,519
looking down on worldly things.

392
00:22:46,880 --> 00:22:49,000
They take risks and betray the organization

393
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:51,039
purely for self-actualization,

394
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:53,559
savoring the thrill of controlling the game

395
00:22:53,880 --> 00:22:55,279
and manipulating others.

396
00:22:58,799 --> 00:23:00,279
You think he's that kind of person?

397
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:04,119
Nobody knows him better than I do.

398
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:07,200
If he becomes a traitor,

399
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:09,960
he'll definitely be the hardest to deal with.

400
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:19,319
How did that test I submitted turn out?

401
00:23:19,480 --> 00:23:20,000
It's ready.

402
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:21,119
Just a moment.

403
00:23:24,079 --> 00:23:25,759
Wasn't it already tested years ago?

404
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:27,960
Well, the technology has improved,

405
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:29,519
so I wanted to see if there were any new findings.

406
00:23:30,119 --> 00:23:31,400
Even the best tech can't do everything.

407
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:31,839
Here you go.

408
00:23:32,160 --> 00:23:32,960
Thanks.

409
00:23:35,079 --> 00:23:35,759
I'll get back to work.

410
00:25:31,680 --> 00:25:32,839
Brother Qi

411
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:05,640
Looking for it or looking for me?

412
00:26:10,799 --> 00:26:12,359
Weren't you right behind me?

413
00:26:12,599 --> 00:26:13,759
I lost sight of you just now.

414
00:26:14,160 --> 00:26:15,400
You were tailing me and still missed me?

415
00:26:15,720 --> 00:26:17,319
Then your years on the job were for nothing.

416
00:26:18,359 --> 00:26:20,799
I'm clumsy. I can't help losing people.

417
00:26:21,279 --> 00:26:22,799
All I know is how to latch onto someone.

418
00:26:24,960 --> 00:26:26,559
Brother Qi, you know all the tricks.

419
00:26:26,559 --> 00:26:27,359
Teach me a thing or two.

420
00:26:28,039 --> 00:26:29,319
I've taught you everything I should.

421
00:26:29,319 --> 00:26:30,680
If you can't learn, more teaching won't help.

422
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:32,960
A lot of things can't be put into words.

423
00:26:33,160 --> 00:26:35,119
Anything you can explain isn't real skill.

424
00:26:35,799 --> 00:26:37,880
You understand it; you're just playing dumb.

425
00:26:38,799 --> 00:26:40,200
Without your guidance,

426
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:42,000
I'd still be clueless even when I'm old.

427
00:26:42,559 --> 00:26:43,200
I mean it.

428
00:26:43,359 --> 00:26:45,680
If you can say it out loud, is it really sincere?

429
00:26:49,240 --> 00:26:50,039
Brother Qi.

430
00:26:51,319 --> 00:26:51,880
Let's chat.

431
00:26:55,880 --> 00:26:57,279
What did the leadership order?

432
00:27:04,920 --> 00:27:06,880
It really is orders from above.

433
00:27:06,880 --> 00:27:08,160
Old Wu came looking for me specifically.

434
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:09,279
Remember that guy?

435
00:27:09,279 --> 00:27:11,359
The one who ran the casino at the antique market.

436
00:27:11,359 --> 00:27:12,319
The one doing real estate now.

437
00:27:12,319 --> 00:27:13,279
Do you remember him?

438
00:27:14,519 --> 00:27:15,839
They call him A-Cai. What about him?

439
00:27:20,079 --> 00:27:20,759
Brother Qi.

440
00:27:20,759 --> 00:27:21,720
This guy...

441
00:27:21,720 --> 00:27:24,240
He used to deal in low-level intel.

442
00:27:24,480 --> 00:27:25,640
Never amounted to anything.

443
00:27:25,640 --> 00:27:27,319
A small fry who couldn't stand scrutiny.

444
00:27:27,319 --> 00:27:28,880
But after two years,

445
00:27:28,880 --> 00:27:29,640
he's stepped up his game.

446
00:27:29,880 --> 00:27:31,720
He's been traveling frequently

447
00:27:31,720 --> 00:27:33,480
between Hong Kong, Macao, Taiwan, China, and here.

448
00:27:33,480 --> 00:27:36,119
Tons of cash moving in and out fast.

449
00:27:36,119 --> 00:27:37,640
Meeting people at midnight, real shady.

450
00:27:37,960 --> 00:27:39,759
He's got over a dozen SIM cards alone.

451
00:27:40,039 --> 00:27:41,519
He might be mixed up in espionage now.

452
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:44,759
Brother Qi,

453
00:27:44,960 --> 00:27:45,960
keep an eye on him.

454
00:27:45,960 --> 00:27:48,319
When the case is solved, full credit goes to you, okay?

455
00:27:51,960 --> 00:27:52,720
Fine.

456
00:27:53,759 --> 00:27:54,880
I'll start tracking him today.

457
00:27:56,559 --> 00:27:57,720
But on one condition:

458
00:27:58,160 --> 00:27:59,319
Don't tell He Chunxiao.

459
00:27:59,319 --> 00:28:00,200
I'll handle it myself.

460
00:28:03,279 --> 00:28:04,960
The lead on this case...

461
00:28:05,559 --> 00:28:06,759
He's the one who found it.

462
00:28:12,839 --> 00:28:13,839
He didn't tell me.

463
00:28:14,519 --> 00:28:15,640
Not a single word.

464
00:28:21,880 --> 00:28:23,839
Jumping ranks to report it, kissing ass.

465
00:28:24,160 --> 00:28:24,720
That's a good thing.

466
00:28:25,079 --> 00:28:25,839
Believe it or not,

467
00:28:25,839 --> 00:28:26,920
the one who'll take your place

468
00:28:26,920 --> 00:28:28,039
is definitely going to be him.

469
00:28:30,599 --> 00:28:32,039
Jumping ranks is a bit inappropriate,

470
00:28:32,440 --> 00:28:34,039
but he didn't come to me either.

471
00:28:34,039 --> 00:28:35,160
He went directly

472
00:28:36,440 --> 00:28:37,559
to Old Wei.

473
00:29:13,480 --> 00:29:14,480
Brother Qi.

474
00:29:14,759 --> 00:29:15,559
Where are you going?

475
00:29:15,759 --> 00:29:16,559
Why don't you wait for me?

476
00:29:16,559 --> 00:29:17,799
I'll run upstairs and grab my bag first.

477
00:29:18,319 --> 00:29:20,200
Sure, no rush. I'll wait for you.

478
00:30:30,640 --> 00:30:31,240
Have a seat.

479
00:30:51,039 --> 00:30:51,839
That's very good.

480
00:30:54,160 --> 00:30:54,920
Very good.

481
00:30:57,720 --> 00:30:59,519
Aside from Wen Zongshu and Lin Kanshan,

482
00:30:59,839 --> 00:31:01,400
keep an eye on Ma Qi as well.

483
00:31:01,759 --> 00:31:04,960
The more details, the better.

484
00:31:05,359 --> 00:31:06,920
Are they involved in any cases?

485
00:31:11,680 --> 00:31:12,640
More than one.

486
00:31:12,920 --> 00:31:13,640
What about Lin Kanshan?

487
00:31:14,119 --> 00:31:14,920
Has he committed crimes too?

488
00:31:14,920 --> 00:31:15,839
Does it carry the death penalty?

489
00:31:24,839 --> 00:31:25,640
Very good.

490
00:31:30,680 --> 00:31:32,279
You don't have a single detail yet.

491
00:31:32,640 --> 00:31:34,079
Film prices have gone up,

492
00:31:34,079 --> 00:31:35,559
taxi fares have gone up too.

493
00:31:35,559 --> 00:31:37,400
I need money to do all this, Chief!

494
00:31:38,279 --> 00:31:38,799
There'll be money.

495
00:31:38,839 --> 00:31:40,359
Can't you approve some funds for me?

496
00:31:41,119 --> 00:31:42,400
Just approve some funds for me!

497
00:31:43,160 --> 00:31:43,960
Of course.

498
00:31:44,279 --> 00:31:45,200
Just not right now.

499
00:31:45,599 --> 00:31:47,119
When the truth finally comes to light,

500
00:31:47,119 --> 00:31:48,240
you'll take top credit.

501
00:31:48,920 --> 00:31:51,000
Honor, flowers,

502
00:31:52,039 --> 00:31:53,799
applause, bonuses...

503
00:31:53,799 --> 00:31:54,720
you'll have them all.

504
00:31:56,400 --> 00:31:57,559
You'll have them all.

505
00:31:59,200 --> 00:32:00,319
You'll have them all.

506
00:32:05,559 --> 00:32:06,640
You'll have them all.

507
00:32:25,039 --> 00:32:26,160
Long time no see, Boss.

508
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:43,279
Nice photography skills.

509
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:49,359
I could buy them.

510
00:32:49,920 --> 00:32:52,279
Or just keep them for my collection.

511
00:32:52,559 --> 00:32:53,319
How much?

512
00:32:54,039 --> 00:32:54,680
I don't want money.

513
00:32:54,920 --> 00:32:56,000
Asking for money is extortion.

514
00:32:56,160 --> 00:32:56,920
That'd be a crime.

515
00:32:57,279 --> 00:32:58,759
Then you came all this way...

516
00:32:59,119 --> 00:33:01,079
to talk about apertures and shutter speeds?

517
00:33:02,680 --> 00:33:04,559
If you voluntarily trade your watch for them,

518
00:33:04,559 --> 00:33:05,519
I'd be open to that.

519
00:33:07,400 --> 00:33:09,400
I left late today and forgot to wear it.

520
00:33:09,799 --> 00:33:10,559
It's at home.

521
00:33:10,559 --> 00:33:11,440
You can go get it.

522
00:33:13,279 --> 00:33:14,079
Burglary?

523
00:33:15,599 --> 00:33:17,640
You tell me. I'll do as you say.

524
00:33:19,640 --> 00:33:21,039
I'll go to your place this afternoon.

525
00:33:21,039 --> 00:33:22,160
Get the watch, sign the agreement.

526
00:33:23,440 --> 00:33:24,119
Whatever you say.

527
00:34:10,639 --> 00:34:11,480
How is it?

528
00:34:15,599 --> 00:34:17,039
Pour me a cup of coffee while you're at it.

529
00:34:17,880 --> 00:34:19,079
Coffee at this hour?

530
00:34:19,079 --> 00:34:20,360
Aren't you going to sleep tonight?

531
00:34:22,119 --> 00:34:23,599
Whether I drink it or not,

532
00:34:23,599 --> 00:34:24,559
I can't sleep anyway.

533
00:34:32,840 --> 00:34:34,280
Should we try "Autumn"?

534
00:34:36,239 --> 00:34:37,559
Would Lin Kanshan use her name

535
00:34:37,559 --> 00:34:38,519
as the base password?

536
00:34:38,960 --> 00:34:40,880
People's minds work in strange ways.

537
00:34:41,039 --> 00:34:43,039
Nothing is ever entirely impossible.

538
00:34:43,679 --> 00:34:44,559
Hold still.

539
00:34:51,599 --> 00:34:52,199
You're not even married yet,

540
00:34:52,199 --> 00:34:53,320
and you've already got gray hair.

541
00:34:53,320 --> 00:34:54,360
Always stressing out over everything.

542
00:34:54,360 --> 00:34:55,760
What's running through your head?

543
00:34:57,199 --> 00:34:58,039
Let me tell you,

544
00:34:58,039 --> 00:34:59,559
you have some too.

545
00:34:59,880 --> 00:35:01,480
Just don't pluck them.

546
00:35:01,480 --> 00:35:03,119
They say the more you pluck, the more will grow.

547
00:35:04,039 --> 00:35:04,760
Who said that?

548
00:35:04,960 --> 00:35:05,800
Ma Qi.

549
00:35:09,280 --> 00:35:10,199
Ma Qi?

550
00:35:15,920 --> 00:35:16,760
Brother Qi.

551
00:35:23,960 --> 00:35:25,559
Do you know anything about psychology?

552
00:35:26,760 --> 00:35:27,599
Why do you think "Autumn"...

553
00:35:27,599 --> 00:35:29,599
chose a pen name like that?

554
00:35:29,920 --> 00:35:31,400
Why not Spring?

555
00:35:31,400 --> 00:35:32,920
Why not Summer or Winter?

556
00:35:33,920 --> 00:35:34,960
What do you think?

557
00:35:35,480 --> 00:35:37,679
If she's pessimistic by nature,

558
00:35:39,119 --> 00:35:40,480
it doesn't seem that way either.

559
00:35:40,800 --> 00:35:41,480
Lately,

560
00:35:41,480 --> 00:35:43,679
I can hear her talking next door every day.

561
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:46,400
Can someone who talks so much really be pessimistic?

562
00:35:46,920 --> 00:35:48,079
You like talking too.

563
00:35:48,400 --> 00:35:49,280
Are you pessimistic?

564
00:35:51,079 --> 00:35:53,639
I'm just cooped up in this room all day.

565
00:35:54,960 --> 00:35:56,440
I'd love to give my brain a break, too.

566
00:35:57,320 --> 00:35:58,400
Write some poetry,

567
00:35:58,679 --> 00:35:59,320
cry whenever I feel like it,

568
00:35:59,320 --> 00:36:00,360
laugh whenever I want,

569
00:36:00,760 --> 00:36:01,960
just like Autumn.

570
00:36:02,280 --> 00:36:03,519
Even just for one day.

571
00:36:03,880 --> 00:36:05,239
Isn't that just how life is?

572
00:36:05,639 --> 00:36:06,679
You envy someone,

573
00:36:06,679 --> 00:36:07,599
and they envy you.

574
00:36:08,239 --> 00:36:09,639
Behind closed doors at home,

575
00:36:09,639 --> 00:36:11,199
everyone has a mess of their own.

576
00:36:14,519 --> 00:36:15,360
Do I often...

577
00:36:15,360 --> 00:36:16,920
subconsciously imitate the way he talks?

578
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:20,679
Do I?

579
00:36:29,119 --> 00:36:29,800
Who?

580
00:36:40,199 --> 00:36:41,480
Shut the door and change your shoes.

581
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:52,119
Minzhong jasmine tea.

582
00:36:52,440 --> 00:36:53,360
Rich and mellow flavor,

583
00:36:53,519 --> 00:36:54,639
a bright, clear brew,

584
00:36:55,519 --> 00:36:56,480
and soft, tender leaves.

585
00:36:57,159 --> 00:36:57,880
Want to try some?

586
00:36:58,400 --> 00:36:59,679
Where's the agreement I asked for?

587
00:36:59,679 --> 00:37:00,480
Is it done yet?

588
00:37:00,800 --> 00:37:01,800
Xiao Lu is here.

589
00:37:02,719 --> 00:37:03,840
What is he doing here?

590
00:37:09,159 --> 00:37:10,039
Under the watch.

591
00:37:10,480 --> 00:37:11,920
The thumbprints have already been stamped.

592
00:37:26,360 --> 00:37:27,440
Don't bother looking.

593
00:37:27,679 --> 00:37:28,360
It's a fake watch.

594
00:37:28,360 --> 00:37:29,639
Getting a new one is easy.

595
00:37:29,639 --> 00:37:30,880
Finding an old one is too hard.

596
00:37:31,480 --> 00:37:32,639
Didn't you wear it before?

597
00:37:33,079 --> 00:37:33,880
Don't you recognize it?

598
00:37:35,320 --> 00:37:36,360
Knowing you were coming,

599
00:37:36,360 --> 00:37:37,960
I deliberately sent Xiao Jin away,

600
00:37:38,440 --> 00:37:40,079
to spare you two the awkwardness.

601
00:37:48,800 --> 00:37:49,920
If she doesn't feel awkward,

602
00:37:50,320 --> 00:37:51,360
why should I?

603
00:37:55,079 --> 00:37:56,599
Where are my photo negatives?

604
00:38:00,039 --> 00:38:02,000
It seems he's blackmailing Lin Kanshan.

605
00:38:06,199 --> 00:38:07,920
If he's blackmailing him, so be it.

606
00:38:08,199 --> 00:38:09,280
A pair of scumbags.

607
00:38:16,400 --> 00:38:18,960
This ends right here between us.

608
00:38:19,119 --> 00:38:20,360
We go our separate ways from now on.

609
00:38:21,119 --> 00:38:22,239
Don't harass me anymore.

610
00:38:22,519 --> 00:38:23,480
Can you do that?

611
00:38:25,519 --> 00:38:27,960
What's mine will still be mine.

612
00:38:42,719 --> 00:38:43,559
Chief Liu.

613
00:38:43,960 --> 00:38:44,719
It's Xiao Lin.

614
00:38:45,079 --> 00:38:46,280
Just calling to report that

615
00:38:46,519 --> 00:38:48,360
the robber reported this afternoon

616
00:38:48,559 --> 00:38:49,599
has already been here.

617
00:38:50,280 --> 00:38:51,599
That's right, a watch.

618
00:38:51,960 --> 00:38:52,719
He just left.

619
00:38:53,360 --> 00:38:54,599
Lin Kanshan called the police.

620
00:38:55,559 --> 00:38:56,320
Yeah.

621
00:38:56,679 --> 00:38:57,360
By the way,

622
00:38:57,880 --> 00:38:59,119
he was afraid I'd call the police,

623
00:38:59,119 --> 00:39:01,400
so he forced me to sign an agreement.

624
00:39:02,239 --> 00:39:03,280
Right, right.

625
00:39:03,280 --> 00:39:04,039
I never expected

626
00:39:04,039 --> 00:39:05,840
something like this to happen in your precinct.

627
00:39:05,840 --> 00:39:07,559
I won't even dare do business anymore.

628
00:39:08,199 --> 00:39:09,079
Okay, sounds good.

629
00:39:09,360 --> 00:39:11,000
Please see that justice is done for me.

630
00:39:11,280 --> 00:39:12,159
Thank you, thank you.

631
00:39:12,559 --> 00:39:13,960
I'll buy you a drink another day.

632
00:39:31,719 --> 00:39:32,159
Pin him down!

633
00:39:32,159 --> 00:39:32,639
Let me go!

634
00:39:32,639 --> 00:39:33,440
What are you doing?!

635
00:39:33,559 --> 00:39:34,280
Why are you arresting me?

636
00:39:34,280 --> 00:39:35,079
Police!

637
00:39:35,079 --> 00:39:38,039
City task force. Major robbery of a Taiwanese businessman.

638
00:39:38,039 --> 00:39:38,760
Where's the loot?

639
00:39:38,960 --> 00:39:39,559
Don't move!

640
00:39:40,199 --> 00:39:42,440
Behave yourself. Caught red-handed with the loot.

641
00:39:42,440 --> 00:39:43,280
Huge sum involved.

642
00:39:43,280 --> 00:39:44,239
Egregious offense.

643
00:39:44,440 --> 00:39:45,119
Cuff him.

644
00:39:47,280 --> 00:39:48,320
All right, clear out, everyone.

645
00:39:48,320 --> 00:39:49,119
Nothing to see here.

646
00:39:49,119 --> 00:39:49,719
Just catching a thief.

647
00:39:49,719 --> 00:39:51,079
Nothing to see here. Move along.

648
00:39:52,079 --> 00:39:53,440
Put your shoes on.

649
00:40:14,679 --> 00:40:15,760
Have some food.

650
00:40:16,039 --> 00:40:17,239
I just made it.

651
00:40:17,920 --> 00:40:18,800
I made a lot.

652
00:40:19,480 --> 00:40:20,239
Eat it while it's hot.

653
00:40:29,920 --> 00:40:30,599
Try this.

654
00:40:40,519 --> 00:40:41,400
This one's good too.

655
00:40:44,119 --> 00:40:45,119
Is it too spicy?

656
00:40:46,480 --> 00:40:47,360
It's all my fault.

657
00:40:47,840 --> 00:40:48,840
I put in too much chili.

658
00:40:48,840 --> 00:40:49,719
Here, drink some water.

659
00:40:51,119 --> 00:40:52,119
Have this dish instead.

660
00:40:52,119 --> 00:40:53,000
This one isn't spicy.

661
00:41:02,400 --> 00:41:03,079
You eat too.

662
00:41:23,599 --> 00:41:25,119
I know you're sick of me,

663
00:41:25,400 --> 00:41:27,519
and you don't want to hear this.

664
00:41:28,679 --> 00:41:30,119
But once I say it, I'll stop.

665
00:41:30,119 --> 00:41:31,199
This is the last time.

666
00:41:31,519 --> 00:41:33,320
The last time I plead for him.

667
00:41:33,679 --> 00:41:35,039
Whatever you do, don't drop the charges.

668
00:41:35,039 --> 00:41:36,840
You have to send him to prison.

669
00:41:36,840 --> 00:41:38,679
If he doesn't go in now, he's finished.

670
00:41:38,679 --> 00:41:39,920
If he dares to rob someone today,

671
00:41:39,920 --> 00:41:41,400
he'll dare to kill tomorrow.

672
00:41:44,320 --> 00:41:45,320
I'm begging you.

673
00:41:47,360 --> 00:41:49,239
In... In prison,

674
00:41:49,239 --> 00:41:50,039
use your connections

675
00:41:50,039 --> 00:41:51,239
to look out for him.

676
00:41:51,800 --> 00:41:52,800
He's a fool.

677
00:41:52,800 --> 00:41:54,840
He's clumsy with words and can't speak up.

678
00:41:54,840 --> 00:41:57,039
I'm afraid they'll bully him to death in there.

679
00:41:59,320 --> 00:42:01,000
I know what you want.

680
00:42:01,320 --> 00:42:03,719
I can take the train to my aunt's tomorrow.

681
00:42:07,320 --> 00:42:08,599
If it weren't for Xiao Lu,

682
00:42:09,480 --> 00:42:10,400
right now I'd probably

683
00:42:10,400 --> 00:42:12,800
still be cutting hogweed in rural Sichuan,

684
00:42:13,480 --> 00:42:15,800
maybe with a house full of kids.

685
00:42:16,559 --> 00:42:19,760
I never would've met you.

686
00:42:53,000 --> 00:42:54,599
You're quite a loyal person.

687
00:42:57,199 --> 00:42:59,119
If I ever get locked up,

688
00:43:00,199 --> 00:43:02,000
would you do what you did today

689
00:43:02,000 --> 00:43:02,880
and plead for me?

690
00:43:08,400 --> 00:43:09,480
I'm Wang Kai.

691
00:43:09,480 --> 00:43:11,199
Inviting you to watch the drama

692
00:43:11,199 --> 00:43:12,039
Confrontation.

693
00:43:12,480 --> 00:43:13,679
As for recent business matters,

694
00:43:13,679 --> 00:43:15,320
don't mention them to He Chunxiao yet.

695
00:43:15,320 --> 00:43:16,639
The kid has gotten ambitious.

696
00:43:16,639 --> 00:43:17,519
He wants to go solo.

697
00:43:19,079 --> 00:43:20,000
Right, this is the car.

698
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:21,000
8395.

699
00:43:22,239 --> 00:43:22,960
I'm on a mission.

700
00:43:23,239 --> 00:43:24,519
I'm catching spies.

701
00:43:24,519 --> 00:43:26,119
You can check the files I kept.

702
00:43:26,119 --> 00:43:27,159
I'm not a fraud.

703
00:43:27,159 --> 00:43:28,760
I really do have intelligence analyses.

704
00:43:29,119 --> 00:43:31,000
He's an absolute fraud.

705
00:43:31,000 --> 00:43:32,400
A fake soldier.

706
00:43:32,400 --> 00:43:33,360
You don't believe me,

707
00:43:33,360 --> 00:43:34,280
and would rather believe

708
00:43:34,280 --> 00:43:35,159
a sick, drug-addicted

709
00:43:35,159 --> 00:43:36,679
fraud full of delusions!
